@* The same thing said plainly: there is no two-thumb control here, and the reason is that
   <input type="range"> has one. Rebuilding it would mean rebuilding the drag, the arrow keys, the
   step grid and the announcement — which is exactly the code the platform is being used to avoid. *@
<div class="flex w-[420px] flex-col gap-3">
    <Slider name="from" Min="0" Max="100" Value="25" aria-label="From" />
    <Slider name="to" Min="0" Max="100" Value="75" aria-label="To" />
    <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
        Two named inputs. The server reads <code>from</code> and <code>to</code>.
    </p>
</div>
